WEBVTT

00:00:00.496 --> 00:00:02.735
Rank your organs. Decide
which matters most,

00:00:02.735 --> 00:00:04.211
and which one you could
lose.

00:00:04.211 --> 00:00:05.382
Two thousand years ago,

00:00:05.382 --> 00:00:07.570
an emperor asked a
physician that question,

00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:09.504
and what he got back was
a government.

00:00:10.052 --> 00:00:11.890
I want a ranking — every
court has one,

00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:12.974
every ministry has one.

00:00:12.974 --> 00:00:15.000
Tell me my organs are all
equally precious,

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.262
and I will know you have
never once had to cut a

00:00:17.262 --> 00:00:18.723
budget. Which of them is
noble,

00:00:18.723 --> 00:00:19.948
and which of them is
base?

00:00:20.492 --> 00:00:22.438
The heart is the office of
the sovereign.

00:00:22.438 --> 00:00:24.953
The lung is the chancellor.
The liver is the general.

00:00:24.953 --> 00:00:26.281
Twelve organs, twelve
posts,

00:00:26.281 --> 00:00:27.895
and not one of them can be
spared.

00:00:27.895 --> 00:00:29.508
That is the whole of your
ranking.

00:00:30.544 --> 00:00:31.848
A granary and a general.

00:00:31.848 --> 00:00:34.620
An envoy who carries joy
and a district office that

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:35.326
stores water.

00:00:35.326 --> 00:00:37.935
Eleven titles for twelve
organs and one ministry

00:00:37.935 --> 00:00:39.457
with a name and no
building.

00:00:40.162 --> 00:00:41.433
I have checked this list
twice,

00:00:41.433 --> 00:00:43.278
and I will now say the part
nobody else will.

00:00:43.278 --> 00:00:44.877
This council has no seat
for the brain.

00:00:44.877 --> 00:00:46.312
Not a junior post, not a
clerkship,

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:47.296
not a single line of it.

00:00:47.296 --> 00:00:49.059
The brain is simply not in
this government,

00:00:49.059 --> 00:00:49.838
at any rank at all.

00:00:50.206 --> 00:00:52.261
Then the physician turns
to the throne.

00:00:52.261 --> 00:00:54.789
An unclear ruler, he says,
endangers all twelve.

00:00:54.789 --> 00:00:56.475
The Emperor fasted, chose
a day,

00:00:56.475 --> 00:00:58.740
and locked the text in a
room. Suwen eight.

00:00:58.740 --> 00:00:59.794
The Numinous Orchid.

00:01:00.385 --> 00:01:03.159
A dramatized adaptation of
a classical philosophical

00:01:03.159 --> 00:01:04.493
text. Not medical advice.

00:01:04.493 --> 00:01:06.841
The full episode asks what
a metaphor costs,

00:01:06.841 --> 00:01:08.922
once it has become too
good to give up,

00:01:08.922 --> 00:01:09.616
and who pays.
